import painting.dl
import ../input.dl

to read breakout input from {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    close a game from view
    if view's input kind = 9:
        if view's key press is one of [the UI space key, the UI R key]:
            set view's key press to -1
        return nothing
    if view's input kind != 3:
        return nothing
    set session to the breakout in (view's instance)
    if view's key press = the UI space key:
        set session's paused to not session's paused
        if session's paused:
            show page "paused" in (view's instance)
        else:
            show page "playing" in (view's instance)
    if view's key press = the UI R key:
        restart session
        show page "playing" in (view's instance)
    if view's key press is one of [the UI space key, the UI R key]:
        set view's damaged to true
        set view's key press to -1

to advance the breakout frame in {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    set session to the breakout in (view's instance)
    set left to (key (the UI left arrow key) is held in view) or (key (the UI A key) is held in view)
    set right to (key (the UI right arrow key) is held in view) or (key (the UI D key) is held in view)
    set machine key 4 to left as an integer
    set machine key 6 to right as an integer
    update session after (view's frame seconds) seconds
    refresh breakout in (view's instance)
    if not session's paused:
        animate UI view view

to play breakout using {a pointer to UI view:view}:
    watch UI input in view using (the function named "read breakout input from $")
    update UI frames in view using (the function named "advance the breakout frame in $")
    run view
